the target language is: lps.

% The promissory note of L4's legal examples (smucclaw/l4-ide,
% jl4/examples/legal/promissory-note.l4, Apache 2.0), written by hand as the
% L4 translator will write it for LPS: the reading of the design notes l4.md
% section 4.2. Time is counted in days from 4 February 2025 (day 0).
%
% Each obligation is a fluent that holds while the obligation is open. A
% payment that meets it ends it, and starts the obligation that follows. As in
% L4, a missed deadline is noticed only when something next happens: a
% payment, or the clock being read ("WAIT UNTIL" in L4). That event starts
% the next obligation and is not itself counted as a payment of it.
%
% Money is in United States dollars throughout; L4's check of the currency is
% left out.

the maximum time is 510.

the events are:
    the note starts; known as note_starts.
    the borrower pays *an amount*; known as pays.
    the clock is read; known as clock_read.

the fluents are:
    the borrower owes *a debt* in instalments since day *a day* with deadline *a deadline*; known as owes_instalment.
    the borrower owes a penalty instalment on *a debt* since day *a day* with deadline *a deadline*; known as owes_penalty.
    the borrower owes all the debts on *a debt* since day *a day*; known as owes_all.
    the note is fulfilled; known as fulfilled.

the templates are:
    *a base* to the power of *a number* is *a value*.
    the monthly instalment is *an amount*.
    the total repayment is *an amount*.
    the instalment due on a debt of *an amount* is *a due amount*.
    the deadline of an instalment on a debt of *an amount* from day *a day* is *a deadline*.
    the deadline of a penalty on a debt of *an amount* from day *a day* is *a deadline*.
    all the debts on a debt of *an amount* are *a total*.

the knowledge base promissory note includes:

% The loan's terms.

a base to the power of a number is a value if
    the number = 0
    and the value = 1.

a base to the power of a number is a value if
    the number > 0
    and a smaller number = the number - 1
    and the base to the power of the smaller number is a smaller value
    and the value = the base * the smaller value.

the monthly instalment is an amount if
    a rate = 0.15 / 12
    and a base = 1 + the rate
    and the base to the power of 12 is a factor
    and the amount = 25000 * (the rate * the factor) / (the factor - 1).

the total repayment is an amount if
    the monthly instalment is an instalment
    and the amount = the instalment * 12.

the instalment due on a debt of an amount is a due amount if
    the monthly instalment is an instalment
    and the instalment > the amount
    and the due amount = the amount.

the instalment due on a debt of an amount is a due amount if
    the monthly instalment is an instalment
    and the instalment =< the amount
    and the due amount = the instalment.

the deadline of an instalment on a debt of an amount from day a day is a deadline if
    the total repayment is a total
    and the monthly instalment is an instalment
    and the deadline = the day + ceiling(((the total - the amount) / the instalment + 1) * 30.436875) + 10.

the deadline of a penalty on a debt of an amount from day a day is a deadline if
    the total repayment is a total
    and the monthly instalment is an instalment
    and the deadline = the day + ceiling(((the total - the amount) / the instalment + 1) * 30.436875) + 30.

all the debts on a debt of an amount are a total if
    the instalment due on a debt of the amount is a due amount
    and the total = the amount + the due amount * 0.05.

% The note starts: the whole repayment is owed in instalments.

when the note starts from a first time to a second time
    and the total repayment is a total
    and the deadline of an instalment on a debt of the total from day the first time is a deadline
then the borrower owes the total in instalments since day the first time with deadline the deadline.

% An instalment paid in time: the rest is owed in instalments, or the note is
% fulfilled.

when the borrower pays an amount from a first time to a second time
    and the borrower owes a debt in instalments since day a day with deadline a deadline
    and the first time > the day
    and the first time =< the deadline
    and the instalment due on a debt of the debt is a due amount
    and the amount >= the due amount - 0.05
    and a rest = the debt - the amount
    and the rest > 0
    and the deadline of an instalment on a debt of the rest from day the first time is a next deadline
then it is not the case that the borrower owes the debt in instalments since day the day with deadline the deadline
    and the borrower owes the rest in instalments since day the first time with deadline the next deadline.

when the borrower pays an amount from a first time to a second time
    and the borrower owes a debt in instalments since day a day with deadline a deadline
    and the first time > the day
    and the first time =< the deadline
    and the instalment due on a debt of the debt is a due amount
    and the amount >= the due amount - 0.05
    and the debt - the amount =< 0
then it is not the case that the borrower owes the debt in instalments since day the day with deadline the deadline
    and the note is fulfilled.

% An instalment missed: noticed at the next payment, or when the clock is read.

when the borrower pays an amount from a first time to a second time
    and the borrower owes a debt in instalments since day a day with deadline a deadline
    and the first time > the deadline
    and the deadline of a penalty on a debt of the debt from day the first time is a next deadline
then it is not the case that the borrower owes the debt in instalments since day the day with deadline the deadline
    and the borrower owes a penalty instalment on the debt since day the first time with deadline the next deadline.

when the clock is read from a first time to a second time
    and the borrower owes a debt in instalments since day a day with deadline a deadline
    and the first time > the deadline
    and the deadline of a penalty on a debt of the debt from day the first time is a next deadline
then it is not the case that the borrower owes the debt in instalments since day the day with deadline the deadline
    and the borrower owes a penalty instalment on the debt since day the first time with deadline the next deadline.

% The penalty instalment: the instalment and 5 per cent. Paid in time, it
% fulfils the note.

when the borrower pays an amount from a first time to a second time
    and the borrower owes a penalty instalment on a debt since day a day with deadline a deadline
    and the first time > the day
    and the first time =< the deadline
    and the instalment due on a debt of the debt is a due amount
    and the amount >= the due amount * 1.05 - 0.05
then it is not the case that the borrower owes a penalty instalment on the debt since day the day with deadline the deadline
    and the note is fulfilled.

when the borrower pays an amount from a first time to a second time
    and the borrower owes a penalty instalment on a debt since day a day with deadline a deadline
    and the first time > the deadline
then it is not the case that the borrower owes a penalty instalment on the debt since day the day with deadline the deadline
    and the borrower owes all the debts on the debt since day the first time.

when the clock is read from a first time to a second time
    and the borrower owes a penalty instalment on a debt since day a day with deadline a deadline
    and the first time > the deadline
then it is not the case that the borrower owes a penalty instalment on the debt since day the day with deadline the deadline
    and the borrower owes all the debts on the debt since day the first time.

% All the debts: no deadline.

when the borrower pays an amount from a first time to a second time
    and the borrower owes all the debts on a debt since day a day
    and the first time > the day
    and all the debts on a debt of the debt are a total
    and the amount >= the total - 0.05
then it is not the case that the borrower owes all the debts on the debt since day the day
    and the note is fulfilled.
